        <button class="btn" data-action="export-sessions" ${state.sessions.length?"":"disabled"}>Sessions (CSV)</button>
        <button class="btn" data-action="export-summary" ${all.length?"":"disabled"}>Species summary (CSV)</button>
        <button class="btn" data-action="export-census" ${state.sessions.some(s=>s.census&&(s.census.start.sizes.length||s.census.end.sizes.length))?"":"disabled"}>Subgroup census (CSV)</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" data-action="export-backup" ${state.sessions.length?"":"disabled"}>Backup (JSON)</button>
      </div>
      <p class="hint">All CSVs open directly in Excel, R, or Python. <b>Bouts</b>: one row per grooming bout. <b>Sessions</b>: one row per session with its duration, scan and grooming counts, and start/end subgroup totals. <b>Species summary</b>: one row per species pooled across sessions. <b>Subgroup census</b>: one row per subgroup with its size. Keep a JSON backup so you never lose raw data.</p>
    </div>

    ${all.length ? `
    <div class="card flush">
      <div style="padding:14px 16px 0"><h2 style="margin:0">All bouts <span class="faint">(${all.length})</span></h2></div>
      <div class="tbl-scroll" style="margin-top:12px;max-height:60vh;overflow:auto">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Species</th><th>Group</th><th>Date</th><th class="num">Scan</th><th>Type</th><th>Subtype</th><th class="num">Size</th><th>Participants</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>${rows}</tbody>
        </table>
